  "label": "Watermelon and Fried Chicken Stereotype",
  "description": "A racist caricature historically used to depict Black Americans as lazy, dependent, or culturally inferior, often associating them with consumption of watermelon and fried chicken. This stereotype is rooted in minstrelsy and has been used to justify systemic racism and economic exploitation.",
